                      (    forth6809.asm):06002                                  ; file), so BPL was testing whatever flags an
                      (    forth6809.asm):06003                                  ; unrelated, earlier instruction happened to
                      (    forth6809.asm):06004                                  ; leave set, not the sign of the value just
                      (    forth6809.asm):06005                                  ; popped. TSTA explicitly tests D's high byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):06006                                  ; (bit 7 of A reflects the full 16-bit value's
                      (    forth6809.asm):06007                                  ; sign) immediately before the branch that
                      (    forth6809.asm):06008                                  ; depends on it. Confirmed via MAME debugger:
                      (    forth6809.asm):06009                                  ; "-123 S>D" returned high cell 0 instead of
                      (    forth6809.asm):06010                                  ; -1 - no sign extension was happening at all.
